      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economics"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economics focuses on allocating scarce resources to satisfy unlimited human needs and wants.",
        "The study of economics is categorized into Microeconomics (individual decisions) and Macroeconomics (aggregate economy).",
        "The four fundamental factors of production are Land, Labour, Capital, and Entrepreneurship.",
        "Scarcity necessitates choice, making Opportunity Cost the fundamental value of the next best alternative forgone.",
        "Economic activities encompass Production, Consumption, Exchange, and Distribution."
      ],
      "id": "5wyn7vl"
